    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30715" root="عنج" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَعْلِ عَنِّجْ</span></b>  occurs in a trad. as a saying of Aboo-Jahl to Ibn-Mes'ood, when the latter put his foot
upon the back of the former's neck; meaning <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَعْلِ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَنِّى</span> [<i>Rise thou from me</i>]; the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ى</span> being changed
into <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ج</span>. (TA. [See art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ج</span>.])

